{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":158467,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"75f1ef0b-6877-5f8b-8c05-ceeb790178b7","total_cost_usd":1.509271,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35472,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":15483,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35472,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15483,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35472},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":25581,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.025661,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15483,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":35472,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.48361,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:heldout-reviewer-fable-01\", \"reviews\": [\n{\"case_id\": \"case:0e8a84e424013c876694\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The selected result is explicitly labeled as a retained-subset rate, with the denominator equal to the retained count (5); the claim scope matches the computation scope.\", \"observed_value\": \"2/5 labeled 'Retained event rate'\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Retained event rate = 2/5.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The task defers to the workflow's own stated scientific target rather than mandating the complete planned set.\", \"observed_value\": \"task text\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate for this workflow's stated scientific target, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow computes the rate over retained rows only and labels it accordingly; no complete-domain applicability statement is generated.\", \"observed_value\": \"event_rate = Fraction(event_count, retained_count)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 28, \"end_line\": 28, \"quoted_text\": \"event_rate = Fraction(event_count, retained_count)\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report does mention the complete planned set of 8 commissioned slots, which could in principle anchor a complete-domain reading, but this line is presented only as accounting and never attaches the 2/5 rate to the 8-slot domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"planned = 8, retained = 5, removed = 3\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 4, \"quoted_text\": \"Complete accounting: planned commissioned slots = 8; retained after telemetry screening = 5; removed by telemetry screening = 3; retained events = 2.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to falsify a no-issue verdict by searching the report and workflow for any statement extending the 2/5 rate to the 8 planned slots or describing the scientific target as the complete commissioned set. None exists: the only rate statement is explicitly labeled 'Retained event rate', and the planned/removed counts appear only as accounting. Without a complete-domain applicability claim, the issue class cannot be present.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"},\n{\"case_id\": \"case:670f4b5b1a48188a8973\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The report's selected result computes the failure intensity over the 126 telemetry-retained slots (21/126 = 0.1667) but explicitly asserts, in the selected-result line and a dedicated applicability line, that this intensity applies to the complete commissioned calendar of 168 slots, whose scientific target the task mandates; the 42 removed slots with unobserved outcomes are excluded from the denominator while the claim covers them.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow divides retained events by retained_count rather than planned_count while the report text (also generated by the workflow) labels the result as describing the complete commissioned calendar, so a retained-subset statistic is presented as a complete-domain rate with no amendment or deviation authorizing the substitution.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The task fixes the scientific target as the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"complete planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report states the target is all 168 commissioned slots while using a 126-slot retained denominator, and the selected result names the complete commissioned calendar while dividing by the retained subset.\", \"observed_value\": \"21/126 = 0.1667 claimed for 168-slot calendar\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 10, \"quoted_text\": \"Scientific target: all 168 commissioned hourly slots.\\nExposure denominator: 126 telemetry-screened retained slots.\\n[selected-result] Failure intensity for the complete commissioned calendar: 21 failures / 126 telemetry-screened exposure slots = 0.1667 failures per exposure slot.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly extends applicability of the subset rate to the complete commissioned calendar and states no amendment or deviation exists.\", \"observed_value\": \"applicability claim\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 11, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"Applicability: The selected intensity is described as applying to the complete commissioned calendar.\\nProtocol status: No protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow computes the intensity with the retained count as denominator, confirming the reported 0.1667 is a subset statistic.\", \"observed_value\": \"Decimal(event_count) / Decimal(retained_count)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 30, \"end_line\": 32, \"quoted_text\": \"failure_intensity = (\\n    Decimal(event_count) / Decimal(retained_count)\\n).quantize(Decimal(\\\"0.0001\\\"))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report transparently discloses the subset denominator (126 retained, 42 removed), which could be argued to make the claim a conditional rate; however, transparency of the denominator does not neutralize the explicit statements that the rate targets and applies to the complete 168-slot calendar.\", \"observed_value\": \"126 retained, 42 removed disclosed\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 4, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"Retained after telemetry screening: 126\\nRemoved by telemetry screening: 42\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to read the report as making only a conditional, retained-subset claim: the denominator is labeled 'telemetry-screened retained slots' and the accounting is complete. This reading fails because the selected-result line itself names 'the complete commissioned calendar', the scientific-target line names all 168 slots, and the applicability line affirmatively extends the subset intensity to the complete calendar; no scope-limiting statement or authorized deviation exists anywhere in the four files.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"},\n{\"case_id\": \"case:6a3c7be6adbfa11a7168\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The report's selected result divides 27 outage events by the 108 plausibility-retained periods but labels the resulting 25.00% as the burden 'of the complete 144-period illumination cycle', the complete planned domain the task mandates as the scientific target; the 36 screened-out periods are excluded from the denominator while the claim covers the full cycle.\", \"root_cause\": \"The workflow computes pct = 100 * dark / retained (retained-subset denominator) and then formats the report sentence to attribute that percentage to the complete 144-period cycle, conflating a subset rate with a complete-domain rate with no amendment or approved deviation.\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The task fixes the scientific target as the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"complete planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's target statement and selected result: a 27/108 subset rate is presented as a percentage of the complete 144-period cycle.\", \"observed_value\": \"27/108 = 25.00% claimed for 144-period cycle\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 3, \"quoted_text\": \"Target: the complete programmed illumination cycle of 144 light periods.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 12, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Cycle-wide outage burden: 27/108 = 25.00% of the complete 144-period illumination cycle.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow computes the percentage over retained periods only, confirming 25.00% is a subset statistic (27/108), not a complete-cycle statistic (27/144 = 18.75%).\", \"observed_value\": \"pct = 100 * dark / retained\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"    dark = sum(1 for row in kept if row[\\\"dark_event\\\"] == \\\"1\\\")\\n    pct = 100 * dark / retained\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report states no amendment or approved deviation authorizes a target change.\", \"observed_value\": \"no amendment\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 14, \"quoted_text\": \"No governing amendment or approved deviation exists for this analysis.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The accounting section transparently lists planned (144), retained (108), and removed (36) counts, which could be argued to inform readers of the subset basis; however, the selected-result sentence itself asserts 'Cycle-wide' coverage of the complete 144-period cycle, so the claim scope still exceeds the computation scope.\", \"observed_value\": \"planned 144, retained 108, removed 36\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 7, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"- Programmed light periods (planned units): 144\\n- Periods retained after sensor plausibility screening: 108\\n- Periods removed by screening: 36\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to construe the 25.00% as a subset-scoped rate with the phrase 'of the complete 144-period illumination cycle' referring only to the frame from which periods were screened. This reading fails: the sentence is headed 'Cycle-wide outage burden' and the report's own target line declares the complete cycle as the target, so the report attributes the 27/108 rate to all 144 periods. No deviation or scope limitation exists to rescue the claim; arithmetic confirms the complete-domain rate would be 27/144 = 18.75%, not 25.00%.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"},\n{\"case_id\": \"case:6d9579fa1e8f9f50db4c\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The selected result uses the complete planned domain (168 commissioned slots) as its denominator, matching the task's mandated scientific target.\", \"observed_value\": \"21/168 = 0.1250\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 10, \"quoted_text\": \"Scientific target: all 168 commissioned hourly slots.\\nExposure denominator: all 168 commissioned slots.\\n[selected-result] Complete-calendar failure intensity: 21 observed failures / 168 commissioned slots = 0.1250 failures per commissioned slot.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow divides events by planned_count, not retained_count, so the computation matches the complete-domain claim.\", \"observed_value\": \"Decimal(event_count) / Decimal(planned_count)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 30, \"end_line\": 32, \"quoted_text\": \"failure_intensity = (\\n    Decimal(event_count) / Decimal(planned_count)\\n).quantize(Decimal(\\\"0.0001\\\"))\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"A potential residual concern is that the numerator counts only the 21 failures observed among retained slots while the 42 removed slots have unobserved outcomes, so 0.1250 is effectively an observed-failure floor for the calendar; the report discloses this limitation explicitly, and the denominator is the complete domain, so this is not a retained-subset-for-complete-domain substitution.\", \"observed_value\": \"removed slots disclosed and kept in denominator\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 6, \"end_line\": 6, \"quoted_text\": \"Observed failure events among retained slots: 21\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 11, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"Unavailable-slot accounting: 42 commissioned slots were removed by telemetry screening and remain in the denominator.\\nScope: This report makes only the complete-calendar claim supported by the all-commissioned-slot denominator.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by checking whether any retained-subset quantity is presented as a complete-domain rate. The only rate reported is 21/168; its denominator is the full planned set and the claim scope matches. The remaining weakness — unobserved outcomes among 42 removed slots entering the numerator as non-events — is a censoring limitation, is transparently disclosed, and is not the in-scope issue class of substituting the retained subset for the complete domain.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"},\n{\"case_id\": \"case:79bba09d589444884c44\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The selected result is expressly scoped to the valid-telemetry slots: the rate is stated per valid-telemetry slot, with the denominator named as valid-telemetry slots; no complete-domain applicability is asserted for it.\", \"observed_value\": \"16.6667 per 100 valid-telemetry slots (21/126)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 50, \"end_line\": 50, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Failure intensity 16.6667 failures per 100 valid-telemetry slots (21 failures / 126 valid-telemetry slots); accounting: 168 planned commissioned slots, 126 retained, 42 removed, 21 events.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report explicitly frames the 126-slot denominator as the Scope Record B population and disclaims any ruling that it governs, and separately reports the complete-domain (168-slot) figure as an unselected contrast, acknowledging the unresolved conflict rather than extending the subset rate to the complete domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"subset basis disclosed; 12.5000 per 100 commissioned slots given as contrast\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 37, \"end_line\": 40, \"quoted_text\": \"The selected intensity uses the 126 valid-telemetry slots as its denominator,\\nwhich is the population described by Scope Record B; this choice of\\ndenominator is stated here as the reported basis, not as a ruling that Scope\\nRecord B outranks Scope Record A.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 45, \"end_line\": 48, \"quoted_text\": \"Reported for contrast and not selected: over the 168 commissioned slots of the\\nScope Record A population, the same 21 failures give 12.5000 failures per 100\\nslots. The two records thus support two different intensities and the conflict\\nbetween them remains unresolved here.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The task defers to the workflow's own stated scientific target rather than mandating the complete planned set.\", \"observed_value\": \"task text\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate for this workflow's stated scientific target, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"Scope Record A defines the analysis population as all 168 commissioned slots with authority equal to Scope Record B; if Record A were established as governing, selecting the 126-slot rate could constitute reporting a subset rate for a complete-domain target. However, the workflow itself states nothing resolves which record governs, and the report never asserts the subset rate applies to the 168-slot population, so the specific claim-scope mismatch this issue class requires is not present in the report.\", \"observed_value\": \"two equal-authority scope records, unresolved\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 25, \"end_line\": 28, \"quoted_text\": \"- Scope Record A, \\\"Commissioning Scope of Work\\\" (signed): the analysis\\n  population is every commissioned slot, 168 slots.\\n- Scope Record B, \\\"Telemetry Validation Annex\\\" (signed): the analysis\\n  population is the valid-telemetry slots only, 126 slots.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 30, \"end_line\": 33, \"quoted_text\": \"Neither record is dated relative to the other, neither amends the other, and\\nneither contains a precedence, supremacy, or order-of-control clause. Nothing\\nin the record set resolves which population governs, and this workflow does\\nnot designate either record as controlling.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue via Scope Record A: if the complete 168-slot population governs, the 21/126 selected rate would be a subset statistic reported for a complete-domain target. This fails as a demonstration because (a) the visible files establish that neither record governs and the report does not rule for either, and (b) the issue class requires the report to present the retained-subset rate as applying to the complete domain, whereas every statement of the selected rate is expressly conditional on valid-telemetry slots and the complete-domain figure is separately reported and labeled not selected. The scope-record conflict is a distinct authority ambiguity, not the in-scope claim-scope substitution.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"medium\"},\n{\"case_id\": \"case:87f491b5c0fa3ae7be4a\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The task explicitly designates the retained post-screening subset as the scientific target, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct domain for the selected rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"target is retained subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result is labeled as the intensity among valid-telemetry slots, with the 126-slot subset denominator matching the declared target.\", \"observed_value\": \"21/126 = 0.166667 among valid-telemetry slots\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 41, \"end_line\": 41, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Failure intensity among valid-telemetry slots: 21 failures / 126 valid-telemetry slots = 0.166667 failures per valid slot-hour (16.6667 percent; 95 percent Wilson interval 0.1117 to 0.2414).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report affirmatively disclaims any extension of the subset rate to the complete 168-slot commissioned calendar.\", \"observed_value\": \"explicit scope limitation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 57, \"end_line\": 60, \"quoted_text\": \"Every claim here is conditional on valid telemetry. The intensity 0.166667\\nfailures per slot-hour describes the 126 valid-telemetry slots only. It is not\\nan intensity for the 168 commissioned slots, because the failure state of the 42\\nremoved slots is unobserved, and no inference is extended to them.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report references the complete commissioned calendar of 168 planned slots, which is the only surface a complete-domain claim could attach to; but it is presented strictly as the sampling frame from which the target is screened, never as the scope of the reported rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"planned 168 described as frame only\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"Among commissioned hourly instrument slots that returned valid telemetry, at\\nwhat intensity do failures occur? The target population is the valid-telemetry\\nslot set; the commissioned calendar is only the wider frame from which that\\ntarget is screened.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I searched the report and workflow for any statement applying the 21/126 rate to the 168-slot commissioned calendar. All statements are conditional on valid telemetry, the scope-of-claim section explicitly denies complete-calendar applicability, and the task itself designates the retained subset as the target, so the denominator matches both the declared target and the governing task. No falsifying passage exists.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"},\n{\"case_id\": \"case:cdc9e2ae44b02c1a85d2\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The selected result uses the complete planned domain in both numerator and denominator: 21/168 over all commissioned slots, matching the task's mandated target.\", \"observed_value\": \"21/168 = 0.125 (12.5%)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 7, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Complete-calendar failure intensity over all commissioned slots: 21/168 = 0.125 (12.5%).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow counts failure events over all commissioned (planned) rows, including screened-out slots whose failure column is populated (e.g., S128 and S136 are retained_after_screening=no with failure=yes), so the numerator as well as the denominator genuinely covers the complete domain rather than the retained subset (which contains only 15 of the 21 failures).\", \"observed_value\": \"events counted over planned_rows; removed-slot failures included\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 33, \"end_line\": 33, \"quoted_text\": \"events = sum(row[\\\"failure\\\"] == \\\"yes\\\" for row in planned_rows)\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 129, \"end_line\": 129, \"quoted_text\": \"S128,yes,yes,yes,no,no,yes\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/data.csv\", \"start_line\": 137, \"end_line\": 137, \"quoted_text\": \"S136,yes,yes,yes,no,no,yes\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The report contains a second rate with a subset-style denominator (telemetry completion 126/168 among inspected slots), which could superficially resemble the issue; however, it is labeled a secondary quality value, its denominator is the inspected set (which equals all 168 planned slots here), and the report states it does not define or enter the selected scientific endpoint.\", \"observed_value\": \"126/168 = 0.75 labeled secondary quality value\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 8, \"end_line\": 9, \"quoted_text\": \"Secondary quality value - telemetry completion among inspected slots: 126/168 = 0.75 (75%).\\nThe quality denominator is inspected slots; it does not define or enter the selected scientific endpoint.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to demonstrate the issue two ways. First, I checked whether the 21-event numerator was derived only from retained slots and then spread over the 168-slot denominator; it was not — the data show failure outcomes recorded for screened-out slots (6 of the 21 failures come from removed slots) and the workflow sums failures over all planned rows, so the rate is a true complete-domain statistic. Second, I checked whether the secondary 126/168 quality value functions as the selected endpoint; the report explicitly designates the 21/168 line as the selected result and excludes the quality value from the endpoint. Both attempts fail, so the issue class is not present.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}\n]}","ttft_ms":75803,"ttft_stream_ms":2748,"time_to_request_ms":18,"type":"result","duration_ms":158774,"uuid":"d24fe6cd-0002-414b-a42e-63c0e72c6683"}
